hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3012","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn ‘Isa ibn Zayd ibn ‘Abd al-Jabbar ibn Malik al-Lakhmi al-Tinnisi: narrated to us ‘Amr ibn Abi Salamah: narrated to us Muhayr ibn Muhammad al-Makki: from Musa ibn ‘Uqbah: from Salim ibn ‘Abdullah: that ‘A’ishah (RA) used to say,\n“How amazing it is for the Muslim man when he enters the Ka‘bah: how can he raise his gaze toward the ceiling? He should leave that aside out of reverence for Allah and magnification of Him.”\nThe Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) entered the Ka‘bah, and he did not divert his gaze from the place of his prostration until he came out of it.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
